From 7387f3861b72ca1b6543faa03d5b7db37f3f67ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:36:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer, utils: among streams in the language wanted, the
 variety wanted goes first (castellano or latino)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CLanguageTag::Matches() narrows a language to ISO 639, so a Spanish track of
Spain and one of Latin America were the same language to the player, which
took whichever ranked first otherwise (the better codec for the audio, the
default flag or the first one for the subtitles). Releases carry both, and
say which is which in the language tag (es-419, es-ES, pt-BR, zh-Hant) where
the container holds one, in curly braces in the title, or only in the title
("Castellano", "Latino", "LatAm", "Español (Latinoamérica)", "Brasil", "VFQ",
"简体"...).

- KODI::UTILS::CLanguageVariety tells the variety of a stream from its tag,
  a tag in curly braces in its title, or the words of its title, for Spanish
  (Spain, Latin America), Portuguese (Portugal, Brazil), French (France,
  Canada) and Chinese (simplified, traditional); a title that names both, or
  neither, says nothing.
- A new setting, "Variety of Spanish, Portuguese, French or Chinese"
  (locale.languagevariety, Player > Language, standard level): Automatic (the
  default) takes it from the region of the preferred language (a language
  add-on such as Spanish (Mexico)) or, for the language of the interface,
  from the region of that language or of the region setting; or one of the
  eight varieties. A variety of another language than the one wanted changes
  nothing.
- Audio (StreamUtils::CompareAudioPreference(), shared with the library):
  among the streams in the language wanted, the one in the variety wanted,
  then one that says nothing, then one of the other variety, before the
  quality. Subtitles: the same among the streams in the language wanted of
  one kind (regular, forced, for the hard of hearing), before the default
  flag of the file. Each stream's own rank, so the orders stay strict weak
  ones; where no variety is wanted nothing changes. A stream chosen for a
  video before still goes first.
- One INFO line per stream chosen where a variety is wanted: its variety and
  why.
Credit: the idea of a preference by region is mephis's (flhs0606/
LibreELEC-Hades, dcfd7435b4, for Chinese); written anew and for the four
languages.
